window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Wildlife photographer Maya Stevens thought she'd left danger behind in the Brazilian rainforest. But when bodies start appearing in Montana's Blackwood Forest... killed in the same ritualistic way as the victims she unknowingly photographed months ago... she realizes her lens may have captured more than just endangered species.</p> <p>As she tracks a pack of wolves for her latest conservation project, Maya finds herself drawn to the enigmatic head forest ranger, Magnus Blackwood. His intimate knowledge of predator behavior both intrigues and unsettles her. But when her medical background as a veterinarian reveals disturbing inconsistencies in the wolf pack's movements, Maya begins to suspect that the forest holds darker secrets than she imagined.</p> <p>With a killer who seems to know her every move and evidence that suggests the impossible, Maya must decide who to trust: her scientific instincts, or her growing attraction to a man who disappears with the moon. In Blackwood Forest, some hunters aren't what they seem... and being prey isn't always a matter of choice.</p> <p>WILD EXPOSURE - Where the line between predator and prey blurs, and every photograph could be her last.</p>"; 
